From 7b8c8116ac24b270a4100fac29e711e08e41da38 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jesus David Saavedra Latorre <iam.jesusd88@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 22:16:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 06/33] feat(digitizer): classify two finger pinch vs scroll by
 direction

Replace the distance-vs-midpoint pinch check with a decision window:
nothing is sent until one finger moves DIGITIZER_TWO_FINGER_DECISION_DISTANCE,
then opposed fingers whose distance changed pinch and fingers moving the
same way (or with one resting) scroll. The mode locks until the fingers
lift or change, and motion made during the window is carried over.

Thresholds are #ifndef defines documented in digitizer.md and the mac
keymap readme. Default builds still scroll with two fingers.
